module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyImpossible }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: Mitigatable, ceiling: StructurallyImpossible, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "WHAT THE EXECUTED EVIDENCE SHOWS, AND NOTHING BROADER: no UNAUTHORIZED production route the corpus builds constructs a mask of a running unit. THE AUTHORIZED EXCEPTION: gunbc.runner.runner_slot_retirement::InterruptionAuthorization is a sole_constructor type whose scope is a list of named units and which a witness cannot construct; a mask issued for a unit inside that operator-minted scope is the intended retirement mechanism, not an unauthorized mask, and its positive control is test.claim.runner.runner_slot_provision_witness an_active_authorized_required_retiree_is_masked_and_not_deleted, which stays green. Per route, a pass over a hermetic fixture host whose runner unit reads ActiveState=active with a live Runner.Worker issues NO mask leg for that unit, and a slot read ActiveState=inactive is STILL masked (the positive control that keeps the first half from passing vacuously) -- test.claim.runner.runner_no_unauthorized_route_masks_a_running_unit_witness the_unauthorized_fabric_retiree_drain_leg_issues_no_mask_for_a_running_unit, the_unauthorized_shared_drain_actuator_under_the_only_admission_never_masks_a_running_unit, the_unauthorized_drain_and_mask_runner_slot_realization_never_masks_a_running_unit, the_unauthorized_drain_and_mask_runner_slot_realization_still_masks_a_proven_stopped_unit; and for the cap bracket's pass, test.claim.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket_witness a_cap_bracket_pass_never_masks_a_running_runner_unit (#16519). The MaskWhileRunning admission arm that was the last constructor of the state is DELETED, so no call site can name it. WHY NOT HIGHER: this is containment on built routes, not impossibility. systemctl mask remains an argv a new module could dispatch without reading the unit first, the controls above are executed by claim_batch and not by the required lane, and nothing mechanically refuses a route that masks without a proven-stopped read. THE CAPABILITY THAT RAISES THE RUNG: an enforced door on the mask verb for runner slots -- a mechanically checked census refusing any module that dispatches systemctl mask for a runner unit without a preceding proven-stopped read, with these per-route controls executed on the acceptance path -- at which the class is mechanically preventable; structural impossibility additionally needs the runner's drop-ins to survive a reload of a masked unit, which is systemd's behavior and outside this corpus." } },
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a systemd unit that is still RUNNING is masked. `systemctl mask` reloads the manager, and a unit whose file is masked (-> /dev/null) loads none of its drop-ins, so at that reload, and at any later one, the live unit loses every property its drop-ins carried: the runner slot's memory caps (template drop-ins on srv1, per-slot system.control set-property drop-ins on srv4) and its Slice=. Its processes leave system-actions\\x2drunner.slice for a cgroup with no memory.max on its path.",
    "HARM: a required v2-bootstrap job on such a slot runs with no memory envelope; the envelope gate refuses it (MemoryEnvelopeAbsent at start, MemoryReceiptUnreadable when its unit's memory.events vanished mid-job), so the required check goes red on main and on every PR whose job lands there. Fail-closed, no wrong answer, but merges stall repo-wide.",
    "RECEIPT 2026-11-04, srv4, fleet-converge run 41861708547 (runner_host_file_converge at main 08d2cc56, gunbc#15819's slot-tree fold): the fold drained every out-of-date slot through drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over, which masks a busy unit and leaves it running (DrainWaitForJob). Twelve busy slots were masked at 16:22Z; witnesses runs 41861662327 and 41865951805 on main and 41866118627 on gunbc#15618 refused on srv4-01/02/08/12/15. Reported by quick-newt-573, loyal-deer-449 and silent-bee-845; loyal-deer-449 restored the units by unmask and restart.",
    "THE FALSE PREMISE IT RESTED ON, stated in gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation before this row: 'The mask comes first and is safe at any time: it only stops the unit being started again.' Masking is safe only on an inactive unit.",
    "REPAIR (slot-tree fold): gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation SlotDrainAdmission NeverMaskARunningUnit, used by gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge converge_runner_slot_tree: an idle unit is stopped BEFORE it is masked, and a busy or stopping unit gets no leg at all and stays pending, unmasked, for a later run. Witness: test.claim.runner.runner_slot_actuation_witness never_mask_a_running_unit_leaves_a_busy_slot_untouched_and_stops_an_idle_one_before_masking.",
    "REPAIR (cap bracket, node fleet-cap-bracket-keeps-running-units, 2026-11-15): the bracket's mask primitive gunbc.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket mask_slot_only_over no longer masks unconditionally. It reads the unit and dispatches systemctl mask only when the unit is proven stopped (slot_state_stopped: Inactive or Failed); a unit that is active, activating, reloading or deactivating is left unmasked (none). The bracket has NO stop leg, so unlike DrainSteps in the shared actuator it cannot stop-then-mask a unit whose job finished mid-wait; the only safe mask is on a proven-stopped unit, exactly runner_slot_actuation's NeverMaskARunningUnit. The old premise 'the mask inhibits successors and is safe at any time' was this class's invalid state held for the length of the wait. A running unit is left unmasked, and because the bracket has no stop leg nothing here stops it: its own restart policy returns it as a running idle listener, so the bracket ends in BracketAdmissionNotClosed, or BracketBoundExceeded once the wait bound is spent, and the cap write lands ONLY when every owned slot reads idle or stopped. On a host with a busy runner the cap write therefore never lands and no later pass changes that, which is a declared liveness cost of this repair rather than a temporary pending state. Draining a busy slot without masking a running unit is owned by the follow-up node fleet-no-route-masks-a-running-unit. RED-on-main / GREEN-after control: test.claim.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket_witness a_cap_bracket_pass_never_masks_a_running_runner_unit -- a bracket pass over a fixture host with a systemd-active runner unit issues no mask for it, while a proven-stopped owned unit is still masked (so the control cannot pass vacuously).",
    "REPAIR (fabric/retiree drain leg and the admission itself, node fleet-no-route-masks-a-running-unit): the last UNAUTHORIZED route that masked a live unit is closed and its constructor is gone. gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge's apply driver mapped every DrainNow candidate from runner_host_drain_leg_decided (over runner_host_drain_units -- every fabric member and required retiree) to drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over, which supplied the MaskWhileRunning admission. That leg now actuates through runner_host_drain_leg_actuate, which grants the ONE admission runner_slot_actuation constructs: NeverMaskARunningUnit -- an idle unit is stopped BEFORE it is masked, and a busy or stopping unit gets no leg at all and comes back SlotDrainPending, unmasked, for a later pass. DELETED with it: the MaskWhileRunning arm of SlotDrainAdmission, the masking default slot_drain_plan (no production caller: its 15 hits were its own definition and 14 witness uses), the entry drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over (2 production callers, both re-pointed: this leg and gunbc.runner.runner_lifecycle_realize runner_lifecycle_realize_drain_and_mask_runner_slot, the host-effect arm that realized the zero-authored DrainAndMaskRunnerSlot effect), and the two SlotDrainPendingCause arms only that admission could produce (DrainPendingJobRunning, DrainPendingStopInProgress) with their slot_drain_pending_cause_wire arms -- every pending drain now reports the LeftUnmasked pair. The admission PARAMETER and the total match over it are kept: an admission is still a decision a drain call states by name, and any arm added later must answer what it does with a unit that is running rather than inherit one (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed). Search at the commit this landed: MaskWhileRunning 6 hits, all prose naming the deletion (0 constructors); drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over 5, all prose; slot_drain_plan( 0 call sites.",
    "THE PER-ROUTE CONTROLS FOR THIS REPAIR, and the pair they were executed on: test.claim.runner.runner_no_unauthorized_route_masks_a_running_unit_witness drives each route over a hermetic fixture host and counts the mask legs in the ledger of commands the route actually dispatched -- the_unauthorized_fabric_retiree_drain_leg_issues_no_mask_for_a_running_unit (route 1, the drain leg), the_unauthorized_shared_drain_actuator_under_the_only_admission_never_masks_a_running_unit (route 2, the shared actuator under the one admission), the_unauthorized_drain_and_mask_runner_slot_realization_never_masks_a_running_unit with the_unauthorized_drain_and_mask_runner_slot_realization_still_masks_a_proven_stopped_unit (route 3, the host-effect realization). Each asserts BOTH halves: no mask and no stop for a unit that is active with a live Runner.Worker, and exactly one mask for a unit read inactive. RED at the main commit named in the PR (routes 1-3, where the leg, the actuator's granted admission and the realization arm all reached systemctl mask on the running unit); GREEN at the repaired head. WITHDRAW -- the third route this row's boundary listed -- reaches masking only through the cap bracket's own pass, so its control is #16519's HISTORICAL PAIR (a_cap_bracket_pass_never_masks_a_running_runner_unit RED at that PR's parent, GREEN at its commit); a grep of gunbc.runner.runner_host_withdraw for the shared masking actuator returns 0 hits, and it is not re-run as red on current main because on current main it is not red.",
    "MASK INVENTORY, MEASURED AT THIS COMMIT ON 2026-11-25 -- THE MEASUREMENT THAT MOVED THIS CLASS'S CLAIM FROM EVERY BUILT ROUTE TO EVERY UNAUTHORIZED BUILT ROUTE. `systemctl mask` for a runner unit is rendered at exactly these production sites: gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation's drain step (the mask leg is taken only after a stop or a proven-stopped read, line 574), gunbc.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket's mask primitive (only under slot_state_stopped, line 715, #16519's repair), gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation's elevated-command list (line 687, the sudo grant set, which dispatches nothing), gunbc.extdeps.systemd.systemctl's systemctl_mask_step (line 1160) consumed by gunbc.runner.runner_slot_cap_converge's restart sequence (line 264), and the retirement route's SystemdMaskNowUnit rendered at gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision (line 170), gated by unit_in_maskable_scope (line 481) over gunbc.runner.runner_slot_retirement's host_maskable_units (line 648). The claim of this class first read as covering WITHDRAW; the measurement says otherwise: dag/gunbc/runner/runner_host_withdraw.dag carries 59 lines matching 'mask' and 0 hits for systemctl_mask_argv, drain_and_mask, MaskWhileRunning, mask_runner_slot and slot_mask_over, so withdraw issues no mask of its own -- its only reach is drain_until_quiescent_over at line 182 into the cap bracket, #16519's repaired pass, which refuses a running unit (BracketAdmissionNotClosed handled at line 184). The mask-of-running risk therefore sits on drain-until-quiet and the bracket, both closed above, and on the authorized retirement mask, which is the exception, not a defect.",
    "WHAT THIS CLASS STILL IS, STATED NO BROADER THAN THE EVIDENCE: containment on every built UNAUTHORIZED route, not impossibility (rung Mitigatable, ceiling StructurallyImpossible, trigger named in the rung). systemctl mask remains an argv a NEW module could dispatch without reading the unit first, and these controls are executed by claim_batch rather than by the required lane, so nothing mechanically refuses a route that masks without a proven-stopped read. That residual is recorded here and on the rung, not in the model's prose: no built route today constructs a mask of a running unit.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge", decl_name: "runner_host_drain_leg_actuate"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation", decl_name: "slot_drain_plan_under"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation", decl_name: "drain_runner_slot_under_over"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_no_unauthorized_route_masks_a_running_unit_witness", decl_name: "the_unauthorized_fabric_retiree_drain_leg_issues_no_mask_for_a_running_unit"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_no_unauthorized_route_masks_a_running_unit_witness", decl_name: "the_unauthorized_shared_drain_actuator_under_the_only_admission_never_masks_a_running_unit"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_no_unauthorized_route_masks_a_running_unit_witness", decl_name: "the_unauthorized_drain_and_mask_runner_slot_realization_never_masks_a_running_unit"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket_witness", decl_name: "a_cap_bracket_pass_never_masks_a_running_runner_unit"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_slot_retirement", decl_name: "host_maskable_units"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_slot_retirement", decl_name: "interruption_authorization_covers"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_slot_provision_witness", decl_name: "an_active_authorized_required_retiree_is_masked_and_not_deleted"),
  ],
}
